Id: time001w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_timesync
Fix: timedatectl set-ntp true, or install chrony.
References: systemd-timesyncd(8), chronyd(8)
Controls: CIS 8.4; NIST AU-8, SC-45; ISO 8.17

No time synchronisation daemon is running (chronyd, systemd-timesyncd,
ntpd or ptp4l were looked for). The clock then drifts, by seconds a day
on ordinary hardware and more in virtual machines, and what depends on
it goes wrong: logs from different machines no longer line up in an
investigation, TLS certificates look expired or not yet valid, and
Kerberos and TOTP codes are refused.

To fix it, turn on the daemon the distribution ships: 'timedatectl
set-ntp true' starts systemd-timesyncd, or install chrony (the default
on Fedora, RHEL and SUSE, and the better choice for a server). A virtual
machine whose hypervisor sets its clock may not need one; if so, accept
the finding with tigris-accept.
